# RULES FOR EVERY AGENT (paste at top of every mod chat)

**NEVER ship lua without syntax check** — `luac -p filepath.lua` must pass silent on every changed `.lua`.

**NEVER claim fixed without user boot test** — zero ScriptRunner popups on game launch.

**Read `re2_framework_log.txt` from the session AFTER your edit** — game install:
`c:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\Dragons Dogma 2\re2_framework_log.txt`

**One change at a time** — syntax fix before architecture refactor.

**Grok before TU 3.1 hook changes** — ask "is this replacement sane" not "write me code".

**Bump version when you ship** — user can't tell what's installed otherwise (`MOD_VERSION` + `modinfo.ini`).

**Your fork = you own the fix.** Don't wait for Nexus authors for GPO / PC / QT.

**If you touch `sort_compatible_gear` or any if/then** — count your `end`s.
